# Environment Example

Copy to `.env` and fill values. Never commit real secrets.

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

```env
# App
NODE_ENV=development
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
API_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Database (example: Supabase / Postgres)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DB
# SUPABASE_URL=
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Auth (example: Google OAuth)
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# AUTH_SECRET=generate-a-long-random-string

# AI providers (server-side only)
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
```

Agents: read this file for required names; never print secret values in reports.
